.TH "HED-QUICKFIX_PREVIEW" "1" "2026-08-11" "hed v1.19.0" "hed manual"
.SH NAME
hed\-quickfix_preview \- When the cursor moves inside a quickfix buffer,
this plugin syncs the preview window to the entry under the cursor \[em]
file, line, and a few lines of surrounding context.
.PP
When the cursor moves inside a quickfix buffer, this plugin syncs the
preview window to the entry under the cursor \[em] file, line, and a few
lines of surrounding context.
.SH Behavior
The plugin registers a \f[CR]HOOK_CURSOR_MOVE\f[R] handler that fires
only when the focused buffer is the quickfix list
(\f[CR][Quickfix]\f[R]).
When the quickfix line under the cursor changes, it:
.IP "1." 3
Reads the file referenced by that entry.
.IP "2." 3
Centers the preview on the target line.
.IP "3." 3
Highlights the matched line.
.PP
If the preview window is closed (or no second window exists), the plugin
does nothing.
.SH Notes
No commands, no keybinds \[em] pure passive hook.
Quickfix itself is provided by \f[CR]core\f[R] (\f[CR]:copen\f[R],
\f[CR]:cclose\f[R], \f[CR]:ctoggle\f[R], \f[CR]:cnext\f[R],
\f[CR]:cprev\f[R], \f[CR]:cadd\f[R], \f[CR]:cclear\f[R]).
.PP
The quickfix buffer is created by \f[CR]core\f[R] whenever a quickfix\-
producing command finishes (e.g., \f[CR]:rg <pattern>\f[R]).
This plugin only adds the live preview behavior.
